From: ArmadaOS Freedom <armadaos-freedom@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 25 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] ThunkLibs/Generator: drop FileManager::clearStatCache for LLVM 23

LLVM 23 removed clang::FileManager's FileSystemStatCache entirely, and with
it FileManager::clearStatCache(). Virtual file entries are consulted directly
by getFileRef(), so there is no stat cache left to invalidate.

Guard the call so FEX keeps building against LLVM 22 (which still has it) and
LLVM 23 (clang 23 in the Fedora 45 builder). Without this the thunk generator
fails to build with:

  gen.cpp:843:10: error: no member named 'clearStatCache' in 'clang::FileManager'

Upstream status: FEX master still calls clearStatCache() unguarded, so this is
carried locally until FEX grows an LLVM 23 guard.
---
 ThunkLibs/Generator/gen.cpp | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/ThunkLibs/Generator/gen.cpp b/ThunkLibs/Generator/gen.cpp
--- a/ThunkLibs/Generator/gen.cpp
+++ b/ThunkLibs/Generator/gen.cpp
@@ -840,6 +840,8 @@
 
   const bool Success = Compiler.ExecuteAction(Action);
 
+#if LLVM_VERSION_MAJOR < 23
   Files->clearStatCache();
+#endif
   return Success;
 }
